## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical debugging in a real-world, multi-region environment with tenant isolation. Emphasizes telemetry-driven root-cause analysis, dynamic traffic shaping, and controlled validation before rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Telemetry-driven debugging across regions
- Per-tenant isolation and rate limiting
- Cache partitioning and traffic shifting
- Progressive degradation with safe fallbacks
- Canary and synthetic test-based validation
- Rollback criteria tied to SLOs

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: rate limiter sketch for per-tenant edge gateway
class RateLimiter {
  constructor(limitPerTenant) { this.limit = limitPerTenant; this.map = new Map(); }
  allow(tenantId) {
    const now = Date.now();
    const rec = this.map.get(tenantId) || { t: now, c: 0 };
    if (now - rec.t > 1000) { rec.t = now; rec.c = 0; }
    if (rec.c < this.limit) { rec.c++; this.map.set(tenantId, rec); return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure success and determine completion of the degradation plan?
- What metrics and traces would you surface to stakeholders during the rollback decision?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to handle multi-region routing faults and basic SRE tooling without outsourcing to advanced chaos scenarios.

## Key Concepts

- Regional observability: latency, error rate, saturation per region
- Alerting: region-specific thresholds
- Traffic control: region-aware routing and small canaries
- Rollback: quick gateway reversion and regional validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lightweight region-aware retry example (conceptual)
async function routeRequest(regionMap, path){
  const region = selectHealthyRegion(regionMap);
  const res = await fetch(`https://${region}${path}`);
  if(!res.ok) throw new Error('Region failed');
  return res;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate that the incident is resolved after rollback?
- What non-functional tests would you run before promoting a region back to full traffic?
